WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:09.410
A study by Stanford university revealed that
in the US alone 3.5 million children and teenagers

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:11.809
are injured playing sports each year.

00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:16.590
But that figure is far greater in other parts
of the world, where things are a little less

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.960
"regulated", and sports tend to get a lot
more messy.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:29.320
Here's the world's top 10 most dangerous sports.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.910
First up is bull running.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:34.780
Known as The Running of the Bulls or encierro.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:40.829
This insane sport usually takes place down
the quaint, peaceful, and extremely narrow

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:44.780
backstreets of towns and cities all across
Spain.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:49.590
Before the bull run commences a large crowd
of people gathers along a narrow backstreet,

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:55.329
then an angry herd of stampeding bulls is
let loose at one end of the street and charges

00:00:55.329 --> 00:01:00.659
down it, mowing down any adrenaline pumped
Spaniard with a death wish who happens to

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:02.179
get in their way.

00:01:02.179 --> 00:01:06.219
The participants run in front of the bulls
and the goal of this sport is to basically

00:01:06.219 --> 00:01:10.780
avoid receiving a nasty bludgeoning of bull's
horn where the sun don't shine.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:16.090
The most popular bull run happens every year
in Pamplona, in northern Spain.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:22.640
Every year around 300 brave amigos are injured
at the event, mostly due to contusions from

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.170
being knocked over.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:31.439
Since 1910, 14 people have been killed during
Pamplona's running of the bulls.

00:01:31.439 --> 00:01:36.140
Imagine if someone told you that they like
to lie flat on a wooden board with wheels

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:42.070
on it and go hurtling down a steep road with
only their feet to use as brakes.

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:46.159
You would probably think they're two trucks
short of a skateboard.

00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:51.500
Well a surprising amount of people actually
enjoy risking their lives, and doing just

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.500
that.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.350
It's a sport known as Street Luge and it's
similar to skateboarding except the board

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:01.609
is slightly longer and the rider is required
to be in a supine position on their luge board,

00:02:01.609 --> 00:02:04.770
which basically means lying down, face up.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:10.759
Oh and to top it all off, participants of
this sport sometimes go down public roads,

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:12.830
with actual cars on them.

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:18.200
When you consider that the rider's visual
profile is only a few inches from the road's

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.010
surface, you can probably imagine the enormous
risks involved.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:28.930
If you think that's scary, it gets worse,
street lugers can reach speed of up to 97

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:29.930
mph.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:34.900
That's considerably faster than a car travelling
on a freeway or motorway.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:39.810
Because the rider's own legs and feet are
the only thing that they can use as breaks,

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:45.670
broken legs or torn ligaments are common in
street luging as well as other, more serious

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:46.670
injuries.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:47.670
One can only imagine the surprise and horror
of the first ever person to partake in street

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:48.670
luging, when they realised half way down their
descent that their only brakes were their

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:49.670
own feet.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:50.670
Needless to say, they probably had a bad time.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.670
Next up is the Vietnamese sport of Hoi Phet.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:54.870
It's a tradition in the village of Hien Quan,
north of Hanoi.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:03:00.430
Each year thousands of villagers gather on
a sand dune and fight over a painted red ball

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:01.430
using sticks.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:05.470
If it sounds primitively violent, that's because
it is.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:09.690
The villagers believe that the ball will bring
them good luck in the new year, if they don't

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:12.439
get their front teeth knocked out trying to
retrieve it.

00:03:12.439 --> 00:03:17.800
At first glance it may seem awfully similar
to hockey, but there are two major differences.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:23.750
The sticks are considerably cruder and more
substantial and it's a hell of a lot more

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:24.930
violent.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:30.370
The participants are allowed to swing their
huge lumps of curved wood at anything or anyone

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:32.519
that gets in the way of the ball.

00:03:32.519 --> 00:03:37.160
Needless to say, injuries are common and blood
is frequently spilt.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:41.909
Funny how hitting people with sticks is not
okay, but add a ball and hey!

00:03:41.909 --> 00:03:42.950
Suddenly it's a sport.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:48.180
If you thought hitting people with sticks
sounds violent, how about hitting people with

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:50.659
sticks whilst hurling balls at them?

00:03:50.659 --> 00:03:54.299
That's pretty much the idea behind Lacrosse.

00:03:54.299 --> 00:03:59.370
Lacrosse is similar to football or basketball
but with long sticks with nets on the end,

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:04.980
oh and there's an awful lot more contact and
general violent tendencies between players.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:09.180
Lacrosse isn't a commonly played sport because
it takes tough and fearless individuals to

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.340
play it at a competitive level.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:16.579
When it comes to rough contact the rules are
more relaxed with Lacrosse than other sports.

00:04:16.579 --> 00:04:21.420
Players are permitted to hit and tackle the
opponents with some considerable force that

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:24.640
would be illegal in most other contact sports.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:30.860
Broken bones, punctured lungs and other serious
injuries are highly common in Lacrosse.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:36.880
Very similar to Lacrosse is a sport called
Irish hurling, which is like lacrosse, but

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:43.790
with axe-shaped wooden sticks, minimal padding
for the players, and it's considerably faster,

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:49.540
in fact is officially the world's fastest
field sport, enough to make a lacrosse player

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.530
shake in their shin guards.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:57.060
Now this next sport involves a bunch of eccentric
cheese lovers who've all had a bit too much

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:03.000
feta for their own good, hurling themselves
down a nearly vertical hill in pursuit of

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.730
a wheel of cheese.

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:10.100
It may sound a bit Emmental but it's a real
sport, and it's called cheese rolling.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:13.560
It take's place every year in Gloucester,
England.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:19.060
So what's the point of all this, surely there's
enough cheese in Gloucester to go around.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:23.060
Well apparently not, the lucky winner, that's
the person that can chuck their limp bodies

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:26.510
down the hill the fastest, get's to the keep
the wheel of cheese.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:29.840
But you can have too much of a Gouda thing.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:34.440
Okay that's enough of the cheese jokes, but
in all seriousness, broken arms and legs are

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:37.490
extremely commonplace during the cheese rolling
event.

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:41.720
It may look like fun, but next time you're
thinking of throwing your body down a hill

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:46.830
after a wheel of cheese, remember, it's a
good deal safer to just go out and buy one.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:52.560
For a long time people would look up to skydivers,
calling them daredevils or brave pioneers.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:58.380
But then in 1978 some daring psychopath went
and jumped straight off a cliff wearing nothing

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:03.190
but a track suit and a small parachute on
their back, and made all the other daredevils

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:04.410
look a bit silly.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:10.880
That daring man was called Carl Boenish and
he was the catalyst for a new breed of sport

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:17.430
known as BASE jumping, a sport which is growing
rapidly in popularity and involves parachuting

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.710
from any fixed structure.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:25.520
The name, BASE jumping is an acronym that
stands for the four categories of fixed objects

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:32.020
which BASE jumping regularly throw themselves
off: Building, antenna, span, and earth.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:37.140
That last one doesn't literally involve hurling
one's self off the face of the Earth, in BASE

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.580
jumping, Earth refers to cliffs.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:45.710
As you can probably imagine the sport is fraught
with danger and fatalities are common.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:51.520
Since the sport started there have been over
250 recorded deaths from BASE jumping.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:58.480
When BASE jumping, technical precision and
solid planning is essential to staying alive,

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:03.580
the slightest mistake, such as steering in
the wrong direction for a second, or even

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:10.000
a strong gust of wind, or if you simply pull
your parachute open a second too late you

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.000
will die.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:14.300
This is not for the faint hearted.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:19.020
Next up is Buzkashi, literally meaning "goat
grabbing".

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:26.240
This sport is played in Central Asia, particularly
in Afghanistan where it as actually the national

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:27.240
sport.

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:32.410
It was brought to Afghanistan by Genghis Khan's
Mongol hordes 800 years ago.

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:38.120
Buzkashi is quite simple, all you need to
play is a pony and a dead goat, oh and twenty

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:41.760
fearless Afghanis who aren't afraid to get
seriously hurt.

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:46.840
The goal of Buzkashi is to fight over the
goat carcass, called a buz, and drag it towards

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:47.920
a goal.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:50.790
Games are long and can sometimes last for
several days.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:53.700
But they are also as brutal as they are long.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:08:00.400
There are few rules and players hit opponents
often and hard, to try and dismount them or

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:02.770
get the goat carcass from them.

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:07.400
Players are usually equipped with whips, which
they not only use on their own horse, but

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:10.840
the opponent's horses and the opponents themselves.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:15.900
It's an extremely brutal sport but it's not
just the players that get injured on a regular

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:16.900
basis.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:22.420
Bukashi games often attract crowds in the
thousands and spectators are at much risk

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:24.860
as the players are themselves.

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:29.281
Several times a game you can expect players
to be flown from their horses and their horses

00:08:29.281 --> 00:08:33.880
to go careering to the ground, often into
the crowd.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:38.829
Spectators therefore have to be constantly
on their guard to avoid being flattened or

00:08:38.829 --> 00:08:41.140
trampled on by a horse.

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:43.909
Or knocked out by a flying player.

00:08:43.909 --> 00:08:48.199
There's no denying that American Football
is a dangerous sport.

00:08:48.199 --> 00:08:52.660
Any sport where you have to wear a helmet
is sure to end in catastrophe.

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:59.069
Since 1931 there have been 1,027 recorded
deaths from American Football, mostly due

00:08:59.069 --> 00:09:04.560
to catastrophic brain injuries from players
smacking their helmets into one another.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:12.240
But American Football is not quite as dangerous
as the sport which is came from - Rugby.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:18.339
Imagine American Football without the hard
helmets, face masks, shoulder pads, and basically

00:09:18.339 --> 00:09:20.810
every other form of protection.

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:27.759
Rugby player typically wear little or no padding,
and any form of hard protective gear is banned.

00:09:27.759 --> 00:09:33.600
Rugby is a rough contact sport and to participate
you pretty much have to be built like a tank,

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:38.070
so if you're no wider than a plank of wood
expect to get knocked into the dirt often

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:42.089
and painfully, especially when you're up against
this lot.

00:09:42.089 --> 00:09:48.180
The two leading causes of death in rugby are
concussion and drowning, no it's not played

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:54.420
underwater, but unfortunately players can
sometimes drown in the mud if they're trapped

00:09:54.420 --> 00:10:00.329
face down at the bottom of a pile up, which
in rugby is called a ruck.

00:10:00.329 --> 00:10:05.580
Next up is boxing, there's no prize for guessing
why boxing is dangerous.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:10.569
Boxing basically consists of 50% getting hit
in the face by a well trained killing machine

00:10:10.569 --> 00:10:13.930
and the other 50% trying not to get hit in
the face.

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:18.519
Obviously it's a brutal sport, but just how
dangerous is it?

00:10:18.519 --> 00:10:24.449
Well a professional boxer can punch with up
to 1,400 pounds per square inch of pressure.

00:10:24.449 --> 00:10:31.810
That's enough power to accelerate their opponents
head at a rate of 53g, that's 53 times the

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.220
force of gravity.

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:39.829
A punch with that much force can cause all
sorts of issues, such as detached retinas,

00:10:39.829 --> 00:10:46.779
brain haemorrhages, fractured skulls and permanent
neurological disorders such as dementia.

00:10:46.779 --> 00:10:55.339
Between 1918 and 1997 there were at least
650 recorded deaths from professional boxing.

00:10:55.339 --> 00:10:59.000
And finally is Horseback riding.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:04.339
But surely beating people with sticks or jumping
off buildings is more dangerous than horseback

00:11:04.339 --> 00:11:05.339
riding?

00:11:05.339 --> 00:11:10.990
Well no, it may come as a surprise, but riding
a horse is probably the most dangerous sport

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:13.519
you can possibly do.

00:11:13.519 --> 00:11:17.529
Horseback riding is not just about little
men jumping over wooden blocks and occasionally

00:11:17.529 --> 00:11:19.230
going flying into a muddy puddle.

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:23.279
There's a lot more to equestrianism than meets
the eye.

00:11:23.279 --> 00:11:28.480
Just staying on top of a horse is a difficult
task in itself, contrary to popular belief

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:33.380
you can't use your hands or legs to balance
on a horse because the rider uses those to

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:40.220
communicate with the horse, so you have to
balance on top of a 550 kg animal traveling

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:46.379
at speeds of up to 70 km/h using only your
buttocks to balance.

00:11:46.379 --> 00:11:53.640
Statistics say that every horse rider can
expect a serious injury for every 350 hours

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:55.050
of riding.

00:11:55.050 --> 00:11:59.999
But it's not just the high frequency of injuries
that makes it dangerous, it's the seriousness

00:11:59.999 --> 00:12:03.459
of these injuries which is truly shocking.

00:12:03.459 --> 00:12:09.579
Horseback riders can their spinal cords snapped
cleanly in two from a fall or their skulls

00:12:09.579 --> 00:12:14.760
crushed under a horses hoof, and that's just
whilst riding the horse.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:20.209
Horses can be unpredictable and whilst they're
not riding them, riders face the constant

00:12:20.209 --> 00:12:23.410
threat of being kicked by a horse without
warning.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:29.690
A horse's kick can exert up to 2,000 pounds
of pressure per square inch.

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:35.970
In fact horses have been known to kick holes
in stable walls with minimal effort.

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:40.639
Horseback riding can be dangerous for the
horses too, if a horse sustains an injury

00:12:40.639 --> 00:12:46.329
whilst racing, such as a broken leg, because
horses are extremely expensive animals to

00:12:46.329 --> 00:12:56.709
maintain, the injured horse is usually euthanised.

